> I'm trying to not pick my nose what do I do when I have a booger
**assistant**:
> You have a few options to consider. You can always use a tissue to gently blow your nose. This is usually the most hygienic way to handle it. If that doesn't work, you can also use a tissue to carefully remove the booger without using your fingers directly. Keeping some saline nasal spray handy might help to loosen any stubborn boogers, making it easier to blow them out. If it's a persistent issue, consider humidifying your living space or staying hydrated to prevent dryness in your nasal passages.
