> why is picking your nose considered unhygenic
**assistant**:
> Picking your nose can introduce bacteria and germs from your fingers into your nasal passages, increasing the risk of infections. It can also irritate the delicate skin inside your nose, causing bleeding or discomfort. Plus, it can spread germs to surfaces or other people afterward. Overall, it’s a behavior that’s generally viewed as socially unacceptable and unhygienic.
